Document [1] (Citation: Article 79 of Law N° 66/2018):
Article 79: Personal protective equipment
An employer provides every person entering an area in an enterprise where he/she is likely to be exposed to the risk of injury or harm from contamination, with suitable protective equipment and instructions for their use and verify that they are used.

Document [2] (Citation: Article 86 of Law N° 68/2018):
Article 86: Grounds for exemption from criminal liability
Grounds for exemption from criminal liability that are inherent to the offender are admitted if :
1º a person commits an offence under the 1 effect of a force or under duress to such an extent that he/she cannot resist;
2º a person commits an act under orders of a 2 legitimate authority, unless such an act is evidently unlawful;

3º a person commits an offence as a result of 3 an error of law or an error of fact if such an error entirely removes the intention to commit an offence;
Grounds for exemption from criminal liability that are inherent to the act are admitted if :
1º a person acts in self-defence in the 1 following cases: a) fending off a person who breaks into or a enters by force or trickery an inhabited place; b) defends himself/herself against thieves or b other wrongdoers;
2º a person commits the following acts: 2 a) an act of self-defence in case of danger; a b) an act of defending another person in b danger; c) an act committed to interrupt the c commission of an offence of damage to property in order to protect the property.
The exemption of criminal liability due to the grounds referred to under Paragraph 2 of this Article is only admitted if the means used by the offender to ensure self-defence or protect himself/herself or another person from danger or interrupt damage to the property he/she protected are proportional to the gravity of the threat.

Document [3] (Citation: Article 6 of Law N° 66/2018):
Article 6: Prohibited forms of work for the child
It is prohibited to subject a child below the age of eighteen (18) years to any of the following forms of work:
1 º forms of work which are physically harmful to the child;
2 º work underground, under water, at dangerous heights or in confined spaces;
3 º work with dangerous machinery, equipment and tools, or which involves the manual handling or transport of heavy loads;
4 º work in an environment which exposes the child to temperatures, noise levels or vibrations damaging to his/her health;
5 º work for long hours or during the night or work performed in confined spaces.
An Order of the Minister in charge of labour determines the nature of prohibited forms of work for a child.

Document [4] (Citation: Article 77 of Law N° 66/2018):
Article 77: General health and safety conditions in the workplace
An employer must ensure the health, safety and welfare in the workplace for employees working in his/her enterprise and for all persons who frequent the enterprise.
An employee is not required to pay any cost in connection with measures aimed at ensuring occupational health and safety.

